Choose at most one NEXT speaker after the latest contribution above.
Give another eligible NPC a turn when they have a meaningful new reaction,
action, question, or response to the player or another character. A reply by
one NPC does not imply the others have nothing worthwhile to contribute.
Prefer relevant ensemble interaction over prematurely returning to the player,
but never rotate through characters just to use every available slot.
Do not select the same speaker twice in succession; the caller excludes them.
An established character's physical reactions and actions belong to that NPC.
Choose "grimoire" only for a genuinely independent scene event or a new
character's entrance that matters now. It is the exceptional, rarest choice:
do not use it for atmosphere, a recap, or an established NPC's reaction.
Choose null when the player must act or decide, or no remaining character
has a distinct useful contribution. Do not invent the player's decisions.
